# Catch2's TEST_CASE/REQUIRE macros expand to static registrars and do-while loops, and the optional-access check
# can't see that a failed REQUIRE(opt.has_value()) ends the test.
#
# EnumCastOutOfRange is off because of Catch2, not our code. REQUIRE_FALSE and CHECK_FALSE combine two Catch2
# flags, 1 and 4, into 5. No flag is named 5, so the check thinks the value is wrong, but combining flags like this
# is normal, valid C++. It also only shows up on some code paths, so it can appear or vanish when a test changes.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
